{"type":"npc","name":"Splintertooth","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":145,"temp":0,"max":145,"details":""},"ac":{"value":26,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":40,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"burrow","value":40}],"details":" (burrow in wooden floors only)"},"immunities":[{"type":"bleed","exceptions":[]},{"type":"nonlethal-attacks","exceptions":[]}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"fire","value":10,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"physical","value":6,"exceptions":["adamantine","axes"],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","shadowtongue"],"details":""},"level":{"value":8},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Old, abandoned houses are the favorite haunt of the insatiable splintertooth. Creaking floorboards—dry, cracking, and veiled in shadow—are their hunting ground. With one careless step of an explorer’s foot, the floorboards split, rising to form a maw of sharp splinters that swallows its victim in an instant.</p><p>Splinterteeth are corrupted creatures of wood and shadow that inhabit the border between the Universe and the Shadow Plane. Trapped between these two realities and unable to fully manifest in either, they briefly hunt in the Universe before slinking back into shadow. In addition to eating living creatures, they enjoy eating furniture. Instead of digesting these inorganic materials, they store them inside their bodies, where they can be ejected at future prey with enormous force.</p><p>It is difficult to spot a splintertooth, especially because they prefer to lie still in darkness. In the light of a lantern, they might appear as a darker patch of wood, knotted and worn. Even when they move, causing the floorboards to ripple, their true form is difficult to discern. Scholars believe that this is because their unique physiology is divided between planes so that only the creature’s face and teeth are phased into reality. If this is true, many of its victims have been ingested into the Shadow Plane, never to be seen again.</p><h2>Variant Splinterteeth</h2><p>Cobblestone, gravel, tile, and even wattle and daub varieties of splinterteeth exist, and all favor dark, abandoned houses.</p><p>These dwellings are often inhabited when the splintertooth first arrives. Once a splintertooth finds a home they like, they claim it as their own, devouring all of the building’s tenants. Nobody knows why they avoid natural areas, but they certainly enjoy tormenting people where they feel safest—in their own homes.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 64/140/250 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing), armor (medium), shield, perception item, skill items (Athletics, Stealth)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> body, bane, charisma, darkness, dexterity, elongating, energy resistant (vitality), sensory (darkvision), space, space shield, spiked, strength, sturdy, tangle shield, throwing, wild, wisdom, wood</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Rodney Sloan","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":6},"dex":{"mod":6},"con":{"mod":2},"int":{"mod":3},"wis":{"mod":4},"cha":{"mod":4}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":18,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"},{"type":"tremorsense","acuity":"imprecise","range":60}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":14,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":18,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":16,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":18},"stealth":{"base":14}},"traits":{"value":["aberration","shadow"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"huge"}}},"_id":"WvNvFibg8kaCDErD","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/splintertooth.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Splintertooth","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"p